{"text": "JACQUELINE TEMPERA\n(908)-907-5405 - jackietempera@gmail.com - @jacktemp\n\nRELATED EXPERIENCE:\nReporter, Providence Journal, Providence, R.1. Oct. 2015- Present\nFile weekly public information requests and use data to support investigative reporting.\n* Test new software and data visualization techniques for the newsroom, filling in as a producer when necessary.\n* Work across and develop sources on many beats, including statewide politics, crime, courts, technology and\nbusiness.\n\nCourts and Crime Stringer, Reuters News, Boston, Mass. May 2015- Oct. 2015\n* Covered federal court and crime in greater Boston area.\n* Monitored local news through Twitter and Reddit to pitch daily stories for wire service.\n\nMetro Correspondent, Boston Globe, Boston, Mass. Dec. 2013 \u2014 Oct. 2015\n\u00a2 Worked as \u201cdrop and run reporter\u201d \u2014 traveling to crime scenes across New England to report for print and web.\n\u00a2 Monitored social media and police scanners for news tips.\n* Revamped training manuals for new reporters.\n\nCommunication Intern, Belfer Center, Cambridge, Mass. Sept. 2014 \u2014 Oct. 2015\n* Updated Harvard Kennedy School\u2019s website with fresh content about international affairs.\n* Wrote feature stories of political fellows and center research projects for the school\u2019s newsletter.\n\u00a2 Edited booklets about the Iran Nuclear Deal, which were sent to members of Congress ahead of critical votes.\n\nManaging Editor, The Berkeley Beacon, Boston, Mass. Sept. 2011 \u2014 Jan. 2015\n* Assigned and edited content for team of 20 writers and editors at Emerson College\u2019s student newspaper.\n\u00a2 Wrote weekly editorials on campus issues.\n\nCollegiate Correspondent, USA Today, McLean, Va. May - Sept. 2013\n* Reported and wrote breaking news stories for USAToday.com.\n\u00a2 Pitched and wrote articles focused on campus issues.\n\nNewsroom Intern, Asbury Park Press, Neptune, N.J. Summers 2012-2013\n* Worked as full-time breaking news reporter, producing regular print and digital content for daily paper.\n* Contributed to food section and weekly travel pullout The Islander.\n\nWeb Intern, Star News Group, Manasquan, N.J. Nov. 2010 \u2014 Jan. 2011\n* Wrote and posted stories to publication\u2019s CMS and social feeds.\n\nIntern, Freehold.InJersey.com, Freehold, N.J. Summer 2010\n* Produced daily articles, videos, and audio clips about local politics and events.\n* Operated newsroom in a local coffee shop; initiative was written about in American Journalism Review.\n\nEDUCATION:\nEmerson College, Boston, Mass. Bachelor of Science, Journalism, May 2015, Magna Cum Laude\nMinor: Political Science\n\nSKILLS:\nExpert: Google Refine, ESRI story maps, Public records laws, CartoDB, Medium, Creativist, Timeline JS, Data wrapper,\nPlot.ly, WordPress blogs, Piktochart, Google (Docs, fusion tables, maps), Social Media (Twitter, Facebook, LinkedIn,\nReddit, Snapchat, Tumblr, Pinterest, Instagram, Vine, Spotify), Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Flash, Illustrator,\nPhotoshop), Audacity, Final Cut Pro, Photography (film and digital), Videography, (iMovie, iTunes, iPhoto), Soundslides,\nMicrosoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Accurint.\nKnowledgeable: HTML, conversational Spanish.\n\nHONORS AND AWARDS:\nRhode Island Press Association\u2019s \u201cNotable New Reporter of The Year\u201d \u2014 2016\nNew England First Amendment Fellowship \u2014 October 2016",
